-football/story/_/id/50510847/ranking-power-4-qbs","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL mock draft: Reid's midseason first-round predictions for all 32 picks","description":"Which NFL team could land Drew Mestemaker? Who needs Chris Cole, Ashton Hampton or Jamari Johnson? Jordan Reid projected first-round picks for 2027 -- and a trade.","published":"2026-11-18T16:28:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50502243/2027-nfl-mock-draft-reid-midseason-32-first-round-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"Jordan Reid","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft: Dolphins, Titans, Eagles, Jets, Chargers in race for No. 1 pick","description":"Five NFL teams have at least 5% odds to land the No. 1 pick in 2027, per ESPN's Football Power Index: the Dolphins, Titans, Eagles, Jets and Chargers.","published":"2026-11-18T13:32:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/50510863/2027-nfl-draft-top-pick-dolphins-titans-eagles-jets-chargers","type":"Story","byline":"NFL Nation, Jordan Reid and Seth Walder","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Anger Index: Why Texas Tech, Tennessee and the Group of 6 should be mad","description":"Ranking the teams who should be most upset about their latest CFP ranking.","published":"2026-11-18T04:25:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50510905/cfp-ranking-2026-anger-index-texas-tech","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4918449/jyaire-hill","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jyaire_Hill"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jyaire Hill","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jyaire_Hill","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:23Z","intro":"Jyaire Hill (born August 31, 2005) is an American college football cornerback for the Michigan Wolverines. He won a national championship in 2023.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Hill enrolled at the University of Michigan as a freshman in 2023. He appeared in four games in Michigan's national championship season before taking a redshirt, recording eight tackles with one and a half being for a loss.\nBefore the 2024 season, Hill competed for one of the Wolverines starting spots in the secondary with transfer cornerbacks Ricky Johnson and Aamir Hall. Hill won the competition and earned his first collegiate start week one versus Fresno State. In week 5 against Minnesota, he had two tackles, both for a loss, and his first collegiate interception. In week 6 versus Washington, Hill recorded seven tackles, including his first career sack. In total, Hill played in 12 games, starting 11 times as the outside cornerback. He finished the season with 35 tackles, six tackles for a loss, one sack, eight passes defended and one interception.\nAs a junior in 2025, Hill started all 13 games and earned honorable mention All-Big Ten. He recorded 36 tackles, one sack and had his only interception of the season against Ohio State. As a senior in 2026, Hill earned the Jim Thorpe Award National Defensive Back of the Week following his game-determining late interception off of John Mateer in the week-two win against No. 11 Oklahoma."}]}}